    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0595" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg501"/>

                <head>No. 330.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 27,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of an
                    affidavit of the captain and two members of the crew of the schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sarah H. Prior</hi>, of Boston, stating the refusal of
                    the captain of the Canadian revenue cutter <hi rendition="#italic">Critic</hi>
                    to permit the restoration to the former vessel, in the port of Malpeque, Prince
                    Edward Island, of her large seine, which she had lost at sea, and-which had been
                    found by the captain of a Canadian vessel, who offered to return the seine to
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Prior</hi>, but was prevented from doing so by the
                    captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Critic.</hi></p>
                <p>This act of prevention, the reason for which is not disclosed, practically
                    disabled the <hi rendition="#italic">Prior</hi>, and she was compelled to return
                    home without having completed her voyage, and in debt.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to ask that Her Majesty’s Government cause investigation of this
                    case to be made.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d330-a1.xml" xpointer="d330-a1"/>
